ecognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x) = \\sin x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1069 "e-760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the sum $1 - \\dfrac{9}{2!} + \\dfrac{81}{4!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}3^{2n}}{(2n)!} \\,\\cdots \\,.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b102c11-e930-5b11-805a-1ff11cdb5995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x) = \\cos x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{1}{2!}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4!}{x}^{4}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{3}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3) & =1-\\frac{9}{2!}+\\frac{81}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{3}^{2n}}{(2n)!}\\,⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\cos(3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1038 