ef3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50922" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f5058c8-bee4-550a-9863-d36cd2227082" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538939 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\pi $ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38c8627e-3005-599a-a37a-fb4e0aa52cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538945 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begi