 of the series $\\,1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b7d68eb-3099-57db-9579-cc9c26274e37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538972 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{{(1/3)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(1/3)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(1/3)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b70f694-75c4-56a5-8060-3f93ae37aa40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538986 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $\\,1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2664ee6-8acb-52ad-889d-ed63a283e637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538998 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯-\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /8)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{8}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{{8}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,1-\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b939d5df-d459-5fd4-9292-d3dcc1c6afac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539002 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83287" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $-3+\\frac{27}{3!}-\\frac{243}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c45730a9-37f0-5369-8e28-cf166dacf491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539007 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3) & =(-3)-\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3 & =-3+\\frac{27}{3!}-\\frac{243}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
